# P-384 field-multiply leaf axiom ↔ fiat-crypto theorem index

Citation table connecting the field-multiply denotation axiom in
`CatCrypt/Crypto/Vale/P384FieldMul.lean` to its discharging fiat-crypto
theorem. Parallel to `CatCrypt/Crypto/KeyAgreement/X25519/CoqAxioms.lean`.

## Field / prime

NIST P-384 base field, `p = 2^384 − 2^128 − 2^96 + 2^32 − 1`
= `0xffffffff…ffffffff0000000000000000ffffffff`. The fiat-crypto
`fiat_p384_mul` is generated by
`word_by_word_montgomery --lang Rust p384 64 '2^384 - 2^128 - 2^96 + 2^32 - 1'`
into `fiat-crypto/fiat-rust/src/p384_64.rs`; the Rust wrapper is
`p384-safe-rust/src/lib.rs::fp_mul` (C ABI `p384_fp_mul`). Montgomery
radix `R = 2^384`, 6×u64 saturated limbs (48 bytes).

## Status legend

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| ✅ proved | fiat-crypto theorem already exists and is `Qed`-closed |
| 📌 cite-only | citation is the cross-prover trust boundary |

## Field arithmetic (Fp_{P-384})

| Lean axiom | Status | fiat-crypto citation |
|---|---|---|
| `P384_fmul_denote` | ✅ proved | `fiat-crypto/src/Arithmetic/WordByWordMontgomery.v::mulmod_correct` (`Qed`): `eval (from_montgomerymod (mulmod a b)) mod m = (eval (from_montgomerymod a) * eval (from_montgomerymod b)) mod m` for `valid a`, `valid b`, at `m = p_{P-384}`. C-operation form: `fiat-crypto/src/COperationSpecifications.v` module `WordByWordMontgomery`, `mul_correct`. Realized leaf: `fiat_p384_mul` in `fiat-crypto/fiat-rust/src/p384_64.rs`; Montgomery product `x · y · R⁻¹ mod p`, `R = 2^384`. |

## See also

* `CatCrypt/Crypto/Vale/P384FieldMul.lean` — the leaf bridge.
* `CatCrypt/Crypto/Vale/SafegcdP384.lean` — the companion Bernstein-Yang inverter.
* `fiat-crypto/src/Arithmetic/WordByWordMontgomery.v` — `mulmod_correct`
